WEBVTT

00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:10.081
Room 11.

00:00:10.516 --> 00:00:11.996
[ door creaks]

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:12.997
Hedwig!

00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:14.303
[ chirps]

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:16.609
Right smart bird
you got there, Mr. Potter.

00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:20.570
He arrived here just five
minutes before yourself.

00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:22.354
[ man clears throat]

00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:23.791
As the Minister for Magic,

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:25.880
it is my duty to inform you,
Mr. Potter,

00:00:25.923 --> 00:00:28.752
that earlier this evening
your uncle's sister

00:00:28.796 --> 00:00:31.624
was located
a little south of Sheffield,

00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:33.539
circling a chimney stack.

00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:36.107
The Accidental Magic
Reversal Department

00:00:36.151 --> 00:00:37.717
was dispatched immediately.

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:42.287
She has been properly punctured
and her memory modified.

00:00:42.331 --> 00:00:45.508
She will have no recollection
of the incident

00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:46.857
whatsoever.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:52.515
So, that's that...
and no harm done.

00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:53.603
[ loud cracking]

00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:54.778
Pea soup?

00:00:54.822 --> 00:00:56.345
Uh, no thank you.

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:58.390
Mm.Um... Minister?

00:00:58.434 --> 00:00:59.609
Yes?

00:00:59.652 --> 00:01:02.133
I don't understand.Understand?

00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:03.787
I broke the law.

00:01:03.831 --> 00:01:05.833
Underage wizards aren't allowed
to use magic at home.

00:01:05.876 --> 00:01:07.095
Oh, come now, Harry.

00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:09.010
The Ministry doesn't
send people to Azkaban

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:10.359
for blowing up their aunts.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:13.536
[ braying like a donkey]

00:01:13.928 --> 00:01:16.887
On the other hand,
running away like that,

00:01:16.931 --> 00:01:22.719
given the state of things,
was very, very irresponsible.

00:01:22.762 --> 00:01:24.547
The "state of things," sir?

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.897
We have a killer
on the loose.

00:01:26.941 --> 00:01:28.899
Sirius Black, you mean?

00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:30.727
But what's he got to do with me?

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.557
Oh, nothing, of course.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.254
You're safe!

00:01:36.298 --> 00:01:37.777
And that's what matters.

00:01:37.821 --> 00:01:40.041
And tomorrow you'll be
on your way back to Hogwarts.

00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:42.521
Oh, uh, these are
your new schoolbooks.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:45.611
I took the liberty of having
them brought here for you.

00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:49.137
Now, Tom will show you
to your room.

00:01:53.271 --> 00:01:54.794
Hedwig.

00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:56.231
MINISTER:
Oh, by the way, Harry,

00:01:56.274 --> 00:01:57.493
whilst you're here

00:01:57.536 --> 00:02:02.193
it would be best
if you didn't... wander.

00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:04.456
[ horns honking]

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.675
MAN:
Right!

00:02:05.718 --> 00:02:07.242
You gonna move that bus
or what?!

00:02:07.285 --> 00:02:11.550
[ wheels squeaking,
train rumbling]

00:02:16.164 --> 00:02:18.906
[ soft bleating]

00:02:23.649 --> 00:02:26.217
[ soft purring]

00:02:27.175 --> 00:02:31.309
[ purring]

00:02:33.007 --> 00:02:36.010
[ vicious snarling and yapping]

00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:46.846
[ yapping stops]

00:02:47.325 --> 00:02:50.763
[ soft purring]

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:56.813
[ loud yapping]

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.601
[ purring]

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:11.697
[ rumbling and thumping]

00:03:13.264 --> 00:03:14.526
[ chirping]

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.964
[ rumbling subsides]

00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:20.576
[ vicious yapping]

00:03:20.619 --> 00:03:23.274
[ whimpering squeak]

00:03:25.624 --> 00:03:27.844
Housekeeping.

00:03:27.887 --> 00:03:29.324
[ wind roaring]

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.021
[ wind stops][ door slams]

00:03:31.065 --> 00:03:33.719
I'll come back later.

00:03:34.764 --> 00:03:36.853
[ door creaks, bangs shut]

00:03:36.896 --> 00:03:39.334
[ yowling, hissing]

00:03:39.377 --> 00:03:40.857
[ snarling]

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.511
RON:
I'm warning you,
Hermione,

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.556
Keep that bloody beast of
yours away from Scabbers,

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.080
or I'll turn it
into a tea cozy!

00:03:46.123 --> 00:03:48.169
HERMOINE:
It's a cat, Ronald.
What do you expect?

00:03:48.212 --> 00:03:50.388
It's in his nature.A cat?

00:03:50.432 --> 00:03:51.868
Is that what they told you?

00:03:51.911 --> 00:03:53.261
It looks more like a pig
with hair, if you ask me.

00:03:53.304 --> 00:03:54.697
That's rich, coming
from the owner

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.525
of that smelly old shoe brush!

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:57.830
It's all right,
Crookshanks.

00:03:57.874 --> 00:04:00.268
You just ignore
the mean little boy.

00:04:00.311 --> 00:04:01.878
Harry!

00:04:01.921 --> 00:04:04.054
We're outHarry!
of gizzards.

00:04:04.098 --> 00:04:06.187
HARRY:
Egypt-- what's it like?

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.624
Brilliant!
Loads of old stuff,

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:09.668
like mummies, tombs.

00:04:09.712 --> 00:04:11.714
Even Scabbers enjoyed himself.

00:04:11.757 --> 00:04:13.672
You know the Egyptians
used to worship cats.

00:04:13.716 --> 00:04:15.283
Yeah, along with
the dung beetles.

00:04:15.326 --> 00:04:16.545
GEORGE:
You're not flashing

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:17.937
that clipping about
again, are you, Ron?

00:04:17.981 --> 00:04:19.548
I haven't shown anyone.No, not a soul.

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:21.637
Not unless you count Tom...the day maid...

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.899
the night maid...the cook...

00:04:22.942 --> 00:04:24.727
that bloke that came
to fix the toilet...

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:25.902
And that wizard
from Belgium.

00:04:25.945 --> 00:04:27.208
Harry!Mrs. Weasley.

00:04:27.251 --> 00:04:28.513
Good to see you, dear.Good to see you, too.

00:04:28.557 --> 00:04:30.211
Now, have you got
everything you need?

00:04:30.254 --> 00:04:31.647
Yep.Yes? All of your books?

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.823
Yeah, it's all upstairs.And all of your clothes?

00:04:33.866 --> 00:04:34.780
Everything's there.

00:04:34.824 --> 00:04:35.781
Good boy.
Thank you.

00:04:35.825 --> 00:04:37.653
Harry Potter.
Mr. Weasley.

00:04:37.696 --> 00:04:40.351
Harry, wonder if I
might have a word?

00:04:40.395 --> 00:04:41.526
Yeah, sure.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.660
Hermione.Good morning, Mr. Weasley.

00:04:44.703 --> 00:04:46.575
Looking forward
to a new term?

00:04:46.618 --> 00:04:49.839
Yeah, it should be great.

00:04:50.753 --> 00:04:53.103
Harry, there are some
within the Ministry

00:04:53.147 --> 00:04:54.713
who would strongly
discourage me

00:04:54.757 --> 00:04:57.629
from divulging what I'm
about to reveal to you.

00:04:57.673 --> 00:05:01.764
But I think that you
need to know the facts.

00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:04.941
You are in danger.

00:05:04.984 --> 00:05:07.378
Grave danger.

00:05:07.422 --> 00:05:11.034
Has this anything to do
with Sirius Black, sir?

00:05:11.078 --> 00:05:13.384
What do you know
about Sirius Black, Harry?

00:05:13.428 --> 00:05:15.952
Only that he's escaped
from Azkaban.

00:05:15.995 --> 00:05:18.215
Do you know why?

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:21.131
13 years ago,
when you stopped...

00:05:21.175 --> 00:05:22.132
Voldemort.

00:05:22.176 --> 00:05:23.525
Don't say his name.

00:05:23.568 --> 00:05:24.656
Sorry.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.051
When you stopped...
You-Know-Who,

00:05:28.095 --> 00:05:30.619
Black lost everything,
but to this day,

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:33.970
he still remains
a faithful servant.

00:05:34.013 --> 00:05:37.582
And in his mind,
you are the only thing

00:05:37.626 --> 00:05:43.153
that stands in the way of...
You-Know-Who returning to power.

00:05:43.197 --> 00:05:49.028
And that is why he
has escaped from Azkaban.

00:05:49.072 --> 00:05:52.162
To find you.

00:05:52.206 --> 00:05:53.946
And kill me.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.644
Harry, I want you
to swear to me

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.211
that whatever
you might hear,

00:05:57.254 --> 00:05:59.996
you won't go looking
for Black.

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:02.433
Mr. Weasley, why
would I go looking

00:06:02.477 --> 00:06:04.522
for someone who
wants to kill me?

00:06:04.566 --> 00:06:06.220
[ train whistle blowing]

00:06:06.263 --> 00:06:08.439
[ people shouting][ rat squeaking]

00:06:08.483 --> 00:06:11.268
Ron! Ron!

00:06:11.312 --> 00:06:13.183
Oh, for goodness sake!

00:06:13.227 --> 00:06:14.271
Don't lose him!

00:06:14.315 --> 00:06:16.186
WOMAN:
Bye-bye, darling!

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.754
HARRY:
I didn't mean to blow her up.

00:06:18.797 --> 00:06:20.103
I just... I lost control.

00:06:20.147 --> 00:06:21.496
RON [ chuckling]:
Brilliant.

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:23.193
HERMIONE:
Honestly, Ron, it's not funny.

00:06:23.237 --> 00:06:24.803
Harry was lucky
not to be expelled.

00:06:24.847 --> 00:06:27.023
I think I was lucky
not to be arrested, actually.

00:06:27.066 --> 00:06:29.634
RON:
I still think it was brilliant.

00:06:29.678 --> 00:06:33.203
Come on.
Everywhere else is full.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.641
Who do you think that is?

00:06:36.685 --> 00:06:38.252
Professor R.J. Lupin.

00:06:38.295 --> 00:06:39.514
You know everything.

00:06:39.557 --> 00:06:41.690
How is it
she knows everything?

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:44.127
It's on his suitcase,
Ronald.

00:06:44.171 --> 00:06:45.346
Oh.

00:06:45.389 --> 00:06:47.217
Do you think he's
really asleep?

00:06:47.261 --> 00:06:50.089
Seems to be. Why?

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:53.832
I've got to tell
you something.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:07:00.056
[ thunder rumbling in distance]

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.713
[ train chugging]

00:07:04.756 --> 00:07:07.106
RON:
Let me get this straight.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.458
Sirius Black has escaped
from Azkaban to come after you?

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.633
Yeah.

00:07:11.676 --> 00:07:12.982
But they'll catch Black,
won't they?

00:07:13.025 --> 00:07:15.376
I mean, everyone's
looking for him.

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:17.029
Sure.

00:07:17.073 --> 00:07:18.901
Except no one's ever
broken out of Azkaban before,

00:07:18.944 --> 00:07:22.339
and... he's a murderous,
raving lunatic.

00:07:22.383 --> 00:07:23.993
Thanks, Ron.

00:07:24.036 --> 00:07:25.037
[ wheels squeaking]

00:07:25.081 --> 00:07:27.257
HERMIONE:
Why are we stopping?

00:07:27.301 --> 00:07:30.173
We can't be there yet.

00:07:33.132 --> 00:07:35.047
[ loud rumbling]What's going on?!

00:07:35.091 --> 00:07:39.574
Don't know.
Maybe we've broken down.

00:07:39.617 --> 00:07:41.924
Ouch, Ron, that was my foot.

00:07:41.967 --> 00:07:47.059
There's something
moving out there.

